    "q-101943": {
      "dom_id": "step-q101943",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14234521/assets/e27737b6aac8caa70549393b78c11ea3d6cc97cb54ec51b557744dfc456359d0.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S=\\{7,9\\}$ and $T=\\{10,25,50\\},$ find $S\\cup T.$",
      "worked_solution": "The union $S\\cup T$ consists of all the elements that are in either $S$ or $T,$ or both. To represent $S\\cup T,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in either $S$ or $T,$ or both.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14234521/assets/34587d9fc3201b9251d233a813d96ed355b8285e64dd1b7d71c72f91c8ee5efb.png)\n\nThe elements $7,9,10,25,50$ are in either $S$ or $T.$ Therefore, the union of $S$ and $T$ is\n\n$$\nS\\cup T=\\{7,9,10,25,50\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
