    "q-102147": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102147",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be the set of all non-negative integer powers of $3$ and the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0,$ respectively. What is $X\\cup Y?$",
      "worked_solution": "The non-negative integer powers of $3$ are\n\n$$\nX=\\{1,3,9,27,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nY=\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $X\\cup Y$ is the *union* of $X$ and $Y,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. In other words, $X\\cup Y$ denotes the set of natural numbers that are either powers of $3$ or multiples of  $4.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X\\cup Y & =\\{1,3,9,27,…\\}\\cup \\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,3,4,8,9,12,16,20,24,27,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-102147-a",
